#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""nersc — drive NERSC Perlmutter from another cluster's login node.

Treats NERSC as one more Slurm backend: the Slurm verbs (sbatch, squeue,
sacct, scancel, ...) pass through verbatim over a persistent multiplexed SSH
connection, plus rsync-based push/pull/sync that go through a NERSC DTN so
bulk bytes never ride the login-node channel budget.

Authentication is a 24-hour sshproxy certificate installed at ~/.ssh/nersc-bridge
by `cluster bridge push` on the workstation, normally from cron. Nothing here
can renew the certificate — if it expires, the remedy is on the workstation
and every error message says so.

Runs on the hub's system python3 (3.6 or newer): no f-string-only
features beyond 3.6, no subprocess capture_output/text kwargs.

Project-specific behaviour (how a submitter is launched, which inputs it needs
staged, what a job return may skip) comes from an optional hooks file named by
`hooks = PATH` in the config; see docs/nersc-bridge.md in the cluster repo.

Verbs:
  Slurm passthrough:  sbatch squeue sacct scancel sinfo scontrol sstat sprio
                      sshare sqs
  sbatch --return [--cleanup] [--run-dir D] [--dest D] ...
                      submit AND register the run dir for automatic return to
                      this cluster when the job finishes (run dir defaults to --chdir)
  track [--cleanup] JOBID SRC [DEST]   register an already-submitted job
  reap [--list] [--max-seconds=N]
                      one idempotent pass: pull finished tracked run dirs back
                      here atomically (run it periodically, e.g. from cron);
                      with N, no new pull starts after N seconds (0: no
                      limit, the default); SIGTERM ends a pass cleanly
  q / jobs            compact `squeue --me` snapshot
  peek JOBID [FILE] [-n N]   inspect a job from here: state + run-dir listing +
                      tail of its output (or FILE) — no paths needed
  fetch JOBID [DEST]  copy a job's run dir here right now, by id alone —
                      works mid-run for partials; rerun to refresh
  run [--cd DIR] CMD  run argv on a NERSC login node (no shell expansion there)
  sh 'LINE'           run a line under `bash -lc` (use for $PSCRATCH, ~, pipes)
  shell               interactive login shell
  push SRC DEST       rsync here -> NERSC via a DTN (cp-like, args pass through)
  pull SRC DEST       rsync NERSC -> here via a DTN
  sync [--dry-run]    mirror the code tree (mirror_src) to NERSC (mirror_dest)
  submit [--no-sync] [--cd DIR] -- CMD   sync, then run CMD remotely in the mirror
  submit ARGS         the project's default form, when a hooks file defines one
  status [--quick]    health: certificate, connection, jobs, mirror age
                      (--quick: this machine only, no remote call)
  doctor              probe connectivity end to end
  config              the effective configuration, key by key
  cert                certificate validity
  connect/disconnect  explicit master control (normally automatic)
"""

